  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Who can reach what",
      "items": [
        "The UI and /api sit behind Cloudflare Access, and the Worker re-checks the token",
        "Writes to /api must come from the app's own origin, and every response carries a CSP and anti-framing headers",
        "Google Home bypasses Access on /oauth and /google, using its own signed tokens",
        "Only the Controller talks to Tuya, using up to two logins it keeps in its own storage and falling back to the second if Tuya refuses the first. When Tuya stops accepting it, the UI shows a QR code and the Controller takes a new login from the scan"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "One brain, one failsafe",
      "items": [
        "The Controller keeps run state and uses alarms for the 10-minute and 5-minute phases",
        "Every open sets the valve's own countdown a little longer than the run, so the valve closes itself if Cloudflare is lost",
        "Each phase change reads the valve back, and stops the run if it was changed outside the controller",
        "Every minute a supervisor closes the valve and ends the run if the valve has been open, or a run has gone on, for more than an hour"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "violet",
      "title": "Weather and rain skips",
      "items": [
        "A scheduled run reads the cached Open-Meteo forecast. Rain, wind, frost or wet soil can skip it or change the number of cycles",
        "Current conditions are a vote of seven forecast models, so one model drizzling on a clear day is outvoted",
        "After a rain skip, the cron tick checks once the look-ahead has passed how much rain fell, and waters in daylight if the rain did not come, unless the next run is close. If the last run was skipped for rain and none fell, the next scheduled run ignores the rain forecast"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "Alerts come from two places",
      "items": [
        "Controller sends ntfy on start, finish, skip and failure, plus a check 10 minutes before each run (offline, low battery, expired Tuya login)",
        "healthchecks.io alerts when a scheduled run never reports in"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "Provisioning",
      "items": [
        "infra/ (Terraform) creates the Worker, cron, Access, the Zero Trust team address and the check; GitHub Actions applies it on every merge to main",
        "Terraform state is kept in a private R2 bucket, never in git",
        "Nothing runs at home: the valve only talks to Tuya's cloud"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "The garden camera",
      "items": [
        "The Worker decides when it wants a photo: 30 seconds into each watering period, a minute after a run, once a day, or on a button press",
        "A script on the homelab polls for that, takes one frame from the Eufy camera and posts it, signed in with an Access service token that can reach only those two routes",
        "A Claude model looks at each frame and a leak sends an ntfy alert with the photo; daily frames become a timelapse",
        "If the script stops asking for 15 minutes the Worker says so, because leak checks silently stop while it is down"
      ]
    }
  ]
